[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Rousseau Gambit"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit: 4.d3 Nf6"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "f7-pressure,piece-activity"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 { The Rousseau Gambit. Black offers the e-pawn to open the f-file and the centre. It is risky, because it weakens the king, so Black has to develop fast. [%cal Gf7f5] }
4. d3 { The quiet reply: White protects the e-pawn and waits. } 4... Nf6 { Develops a piece and eyes the e4 pawn at the same time. If White takes on f5 or lets the pawns meet, Black's pieces are ready. [%cal Gf6e4] }
5. O-O (5. Nc3 5... Bb4 { Pins the knight to the king's side of the board and adds pressure on e4. } 6. O-O 6... Bxc3 7. bxc3 7... fxe4 8. dxe4 8... d6 9. Nh4 9... Na5) (5. Bg5 5... Be7 6. Nc3 6... d6) (5. exf5 5... d5 { Strikes at the bishop and the centre at once. } 6. Bb3 6... Bxf5 7. O-O 7... Bd6) (5. Ng5 5... d5 6. exd5 6... Na5) 5... Bc5 { Develops the bishop where it eyes f2, White's weakest point, and prepares to castle. [%cal Gc5f2] }
6. Nc3 6... d6 { Supports the e5 pawn and opens the way for the bishop on c8. }
7. Bg5 7... Na5 { Challenges White's strong bishop on c4 before it can take part in an attack on f7. [%cal Ga5c4] }
8. Bxf6 8... Qxf6 { The queen takes back and now eyes both c3 and f2. } 9. b4 9... Nxc4 10. dxc4 10... Bb6 *
